  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council (29 divisions), 1958: nominations 20 May 1958; six contests, polled 5 June 1958. The outgoing member in Moyra Castle was deemed re-elected. Labels as printed in the Newry Telegraph nominations list. Polled 5 June 1958. \"Sammon\" in the Newry Reporter, \"Watters\" in the Newry Reporter and Armagh Guardian. The Newry Telegraph and Armagh Guardian call Waters the outgoing member, the Newry Reporter Mallon. The Newry Reporter prints 271 votes cast and 2 spoilt, but the three totals already sum to 271."
